  {
   "id": "b4",
   "scene": "s03",
   "title": "Staid to interesting",
   "vo": "But why? Why would Meta, a company known for building the container, make a character? Meta's naming and look are staid, corporate, clean: a blue logo mark built to sit quietly across its apps. Meta didn't redesign the house to make room for Muse. It let one product step outside of the system, with its own mark, its own character and a name with history. The house stayed, and one product got a soul. One must ask: does every product in your house have to look like the parent?",
